  "limitations": [
    "Universe roster and baseline shelves retain prior HTML composition. Live catalogue data is represented by small sample rails, not the complete franchise catalogues.",
    "DCAU portals and all four illustrated interiors use exact source artwork; scene animation is static. Comic/video IDs are source-derived; unavailable covers use title cards.",
    "Star Wars galaxy is a keyboard-accessible 2D system map, not the native 3D scene.",
    "One Piece East Blue uses original source SVG atlas; other seas use labelled browser-safe route maps. Arc episode/volume counts are explicit representative fixtures.",
    "Cosmere atlas is a 2D six-system approximation.",
    "Standard missing cover art uses explicit typographic title cards, not unrelated covers.",
    "Vault folder selection/indexing, native Explorer, file presence, and identity matching are staged sample states.",
    "Downloads never contacts a provider or downloads/deletes real bytes. Progress is deterministic, not a background transfer.",
    "Universes without a downloaded source banner retain a neutral local wallpaper; their authentic franchise marks are bundled."
  ],
